To add server-side searching for **Batch ID** and **VID** to your VoucherAuthorization.jsx file, you need to follow the same pattern we used for the status screen: update the fetchPendingBatches function to use the filterModel and send those parameters to the API.
Here are the step-by-step changes for VoucherAuthorization.jsx:
### 1. Add Filter State
At the top of your component, where your useState hooks are, add:
```javascript
  const [paginationModel, setPaginationModel] = useState({ page: 0, pageSize: 10 });
  const [totalRowCount, setTotalRowCount] = useState(0);
  const [filterModel, setFilterModel] = useState({ items: [] });

```
### 2. Update fetchPendingBatches
Update this function to include the search parameters in the callApi request.
```javascript
  const fetchPendingBatches = useCallback(async (isSilent = false) => {
    if (!isSilent) setLoading(true);
    try {
      // --- EXTRACT SEARCH FILTERS ---
      let batchIdSearch = "";
      let vidSearch = "";
      if (filterModel && filterModel.items) {
        filterModel.items.forEach(item => {
          if (item.field === 'batchId' && item.value) batchIdSearch = item.value;
          if (item.field === 'vid' && item.value) vidSearch = item.value;
        });
      }

      // --- APPEND FILTERS TO API ---
      const response = await callApi(
        `/JS/voucher/checker/pending-approvals?page=${paginationModel.page}&size=${paginationModel.pageSize}&batchId=${encodeURIComponent(batchIdSearch)}&vid=${encodeURIComponent(vidSearch)}`,
        null,
        "GET"
      );

      // ... (rest of your logic to handle fetchedRows, uniqueWorkflows, and stepsMap) ...

      if (isMounted.current) {
        setWorkflowStepsMap(stepsMap);
        setRows(fetchedRows);
        setTotalRowCount(response.totalElements || fetchedRows.length);
      }
    } catch (err) {
      if (isMounted.current && err.name !== "CanceledError")
        showSnackBar("Failed to load requests", "error");
    } finally {
      if (isMounted.current) setLoading(false);
    }
  }, [callApi, showSnackBar, paginationModel, filterModel]);

```
### 3. Update the DataGrid
Replace your current <DataGrid/> in the return statement with this:
```javascript
        <DataGrid
          rows={rows}
          columns={columns}
          loading={loading}
          getRowId={(row) => row.batchId}
          disableRowSelectionOnClick
          
          // Pagination & Filtering Server-Side
          paginationMode="server"
          rowCount={totalRowCount}
          paginationModel={paginationModel}
          onPaginationModelChange={setPaginationModel}
          
          filterMode="server"
          filterModel={filterModel}
          onFilterModelChange={setFilterModel}
          
          disableColumnResize
          rowHeight={52}
          slots={{ 
            noRowsOverlay: CustomNoRowsOverlay,
