        />

```
### 4. Backend Requirement
Remember that your **Spring Boot Controller/Service** for /checker/pending-approvals must also be updated to accept the batchId and vid parameters, just like we did for the all-requests-summary endpoint.
**Update your Controller:**
```java
    @GetMapping("/checker/pending-approvals")
    public ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>> getPendingApprovals(
            @RequestHeader("Authorization") String token,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "10") int size,
            @RequestParam(required = false, defaultValue = "") String batchId,
            @RequestParam(required = false, defaultValue = "") String vid) {
        
        String userId = jwtUtil.getUserIdFromToken(token);
        Integer userRole = jwtUtil.getUserRoleFromToken(token);
        
        return ResponseEntity.ok(queryService.getPendingApprovals(userId, userRole, page, size, batchId, vid));
    }

```
**Update your Service:**
Inside your getPendingApprovals method, use the same dynamic StringBuilder whereClause logic we used for the status screen, ensuring you append AND p.BATCH_ID LIKE ? and AND LOWER(p.VID_FK) LIKE LOWER(?) to the SQL query.
This will give the Authorization screen the exact same powerful, server-side search capability as the Status screen!
